# Replace Browser Interactions with In-App UI

The goal is to remove all native browser `alert()`, `confirm()`, and `prompt()` calls and replace them with a premium, consistent in-app UI system.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] UI Feedback System
We will implement a global feedback system using Zustand for state management and Framer Motion for animations.

#### [NEW] [toastStore.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/toastStore.ts)
A Zustand store to manage active toasts and modal state.

#### [NEW] [Toaster.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/ui/Toaster.tsx)
A global component to render active toasts.

#### [NEW] [Dialog.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/ui/Dialog.tsx)
A global modal component for confirmations and prompts.

#### [MODIFY] [ClientLayout.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/ClientLayout.tsx)
Register the `Toaster` and `Dialog` providers.

### Refactoring Callsites
We will replace all native calls with the new system.

#### [MODIFY] Multiple Files
- [frontend/app/meetings/page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/meetings/page.tsx): Replace `alert` with `toast`.
- [frontend/app/timetable/page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/timetable/page.tsx): Replace `confirm` with `dialog`.
- [frontend/app/notes/page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/notes/page.tsx): Replace `confirm` with `dialog`.
- [frontend/app/tasks/page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/tasks/page.tsx): Replace `confirm` with `dialog`.
- [frontend/components/meetings/SettingsModal.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/meetings/SettingsModal.tsx): Replace `confirm` with `dialog`.
- (And all other identified files)

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- I will write a small test script/component to verify that calling the new toast/dialog functions correctly renders the UI.
- Run `npm run dev` and manually verify the interactions.

### Manual Verification
1. Open the app in the browser.
2. Trigger an action that previously showed an alert (e.g., saving a meeting).
3. Verify that a toast notification appears instead.
4. Trigger an action that previously showed a confirm box (e.g., deleting a task).
5. Verify that a custom modal appears and functions correctly.
6. Trigger an action that previously showed a prompt (if any).
7. Verify that a custom prompt modal appears.
